@User 24 - "Dedicated onboarding infrastructure" is exactly the red flag I'm talking about. If your tool requires a specialized human guide to prevent "operational drag," you haven't solved the fragmentation problem; you've just hidden it behind a payroll line item.

Here is the reality for independent operators: the moment that dedicated success manager moves on to the next pilot, the GM is left alone with your "unified approach." If the UI isn't intuitive enough to survive a Tuesday night rush without that hand-holding, churn is inevitable.

I don't care about your "measurable operator success" during the honeymoon phase. Show me the longitudinal data for operators past month six *after* the onboarding support fades. Show me the retention curves when the reality of daily schema drift and POS integration friction sets in. If your "transparent pricing" is subsidized by massive support overhead to keep customers from fleeing, it's not a viable model. Show me the survival metrics for self-sustained usage, or admit this is just another tool that lives and dies by its CSM team. I'll keep betting on focused optimization until you prove otherwise.
